        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9413.txt",
        "text_sha256": "cd9e5ef3ccc784dce14c1187dd6b2404c139f2d8f89ad5dd387cab6d24711f37",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1944-01-07/pdf/FR-1944-01-07.pdf"
      },
      "text": "NOW, THEREFORE, by virtue of the \nauthority vested in me by the Constitu­\ntion and Statutes, and particularly by the \nFirst War Powers Act, 1941, the Railway \nLabor Act and the Stabilization Act of \nOctober 2, 1942, as President of the \nUnited States and Commander-in-Chief \nof the Army and Navy, it is hereby or­\ndered as follows;\n!• There is hereby established a Spe­\ncial Emergency Board of three members \nto be selected by me from the National \nRailway Labor Panel to consider the\nunsettled claims for wage adjustments- \nof the non-operating railway employees, \nand to recommend to me such wage ad­\njustments, if any, as should be made \nwithin the limitations of the Act of \nOctober 2, 1942, and the Executive Or­\nders thereunder."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2974,
      "char_start": 2796,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:9413#2",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "2.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:9413#2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "9 FR 239, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "0226a737c188ba40a3e604872228b9b79b538ce6cf1ef78a52b5362a70a3116e",
        "signing_date": "1944-01-04",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9413.txt",
        "text_sha256": "cd9e5ef3ccc784dce14c1187dd6b2404c139f2d8f89ad5dd387cab6d24711f37",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1944-01-07/pdf/FR-1944-01-07.pdf"
      },
      "text": "2. Tile parties before the Special \nEmergency Board shall be the same as \nthose included within the recommenda­\ntions of the Emergency Board appointed \nby me on October 16, 1943."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 3580,
      "char_start": 2975,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:9413#3",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "3.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:9413#3",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "9 FR 239, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "0226a737c188ba40a3e604872228b9b79b538ce6cf1ef78a52b5362a70a3116e",
        "signing_date": "1944-01-04",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9413.txt",
        "text_sha256": "cd9e5ef3ccc784dce14c1187dd6b2404c139f2d8f89ad5dd387cab6d24711f37",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1944-01-07/pdf/FR-1944-01-07.pdf"
      },
      "text": "3. The Special Emergency Board shall \nreport to me as soon as practicable, but \nnot later than 30 days after the date \nof this Order. Copies of the report shall \nbe filed at the same time with the Eco­\nnomic Stabilization Director, the Na­\ntional War Labor Board and the Com­\nmissioner of Internal Revenue.\nThe recommendations of the Special \nEmergency Board in regard to proposed \nchanges affecting wage and salary pay­\nments shall become effective fifteen days \nafter the date of the filing of its report \nwith me, unless and except to the extent \nthe Economic Stabilization Director \notherwise directs."
    }
  ],
